hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1029","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I memorized it on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Al-Araj told me, on the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, h and he told us Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Khashram, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard it from Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, and this is a hadith Abdul-Jabbar, the hadith of Al-Zuhri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led with us a prayer that we think was the afternoon prayer, but when it was the second time, he stood up and did not He was sitting, and when it was before the salutation, he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting.”"
"1030","Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman told us, my uncle told me, Ibn Abi Hazim told me, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who is the son of Uthman, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdul Allah ibn Buhaynah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one of the prayers, then he stood up from two more and recited it, then continued until he finished.” Of his prayer, all that remained was the salutation, so he prostrated two prostrations while sitting before he said the salutation.”"
